# C24: the GROUP-skip fix, priced against the published timing
#   date            2026-09-20T14:40:25Z
#   machine         Linux 6.18.44-fc-v37 x86_64, 4 vCPU, Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.80GHz
#   compiler        g++ (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0
#   commit          a12ae492
#
# The fix changed `ak::Dec::skip`'s SIGNATURE, so every decode function in
# src/generated/core_native.cpp was recompiled and gcc's inlining decisions in that
# TU moved with it (see logs/cpp/boundary.log: dec_list_results_response is now
# inlined into its caller inside the control TU). The skip itself is on the
# unknown-field path, which no payload of shapes.json reaches. "It should not move"
# is a prediction; this is the measurement.

# C24: did the GROUP-skip fix move any timing?
