VERDICT: nothing moved by more than the across-build drift bar, so the
published timing tables stand and are NOT re-taken. The largest movers are
P5.2-P5.4, whose own `pb` denominator has an 11-32 percent round-to-round
spread (STATE.md), so they are where a re-run moves most whatever changed.

===== the fresh run in full, so the comparison above can be re-derived =====
-std=201703  impl=target  guard=on  decode-policy=reject  linkage=shared  rounds=9
protobuf 3021012.  pb = SerializeToString (what a C++ consumer writes).
protobuf validates UTF-8 on SERIALIZE; the spec says the core does not, so
`ffi-valtc` is the like-for-like row and `ffi` is the specified behaviour.
NDEBUG is defined: protobuf's GOOGLE_DCHECKs are compiled out.

